<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan Telecom up 6.61 percent.</title>
<headline>Pakistan Telecom up 6.61 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan Telecommunications Company Ltd (PTCL) rose 1.70 rupees, or 6.61 percent, to 27.40 on Wednesday after its Global Depositary Receipt rates jumped abroad, dealers said.</p>
<p>A turnover of 300,500 shares of PTCL was recorded in early trade.</p>
<p>&quot;PTCL's GDR rates are up on foreign buying as the levels are attractive, which also pushed up its price here,&quot; dealer Mohammad Iqbal said.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192.</p>
</text>
